    "author": "[marvinm2]",
    "comments": [
      {
        "content": "The environmental contaminant 2,3,7,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-p-dioxin (TCDD) binds the aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR), which is held in the cytoplasm by HSP90 and the co-chaperone AIP. Ligand binding releases the receptor, which moves to the nucleus, dimerises with ARNT and induces the xenobiotic-metabolising enzymes CYP1A1, CYP1B1 and NQO1 and the repressor AHRR in human cells.",
        "source": "WikiPathways-description"
      }
